Why is ArrayDeque generally preferred over LinkedList for Queue implementation?
ArrayDeque is generally preferred over LinkedList for Queue implementation because it uses contiguous memory (better cache locality),
has lower memory overhead (no node pointers), and avoids unnecessary synchronization, resulting in better performance.

🧠 Why this answer works

You covered the three things interviewers care about:

1️⃣ Memory model

ArrayDeque → contiguous array

LinkedList → node + prev + next (heavy)

2️⃣ Performance

Better cache locality → faster operations

3️⃣ Threading

No synchronization overhead by default

